From 40e30cf0c5d0ff7e126c39bc2d326f6045e65e4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Sep 2022 11:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 067/841] feat(stm32mp1): always boot at 650MHz

Switching to higher CPU frequencies requires a dedicated chip version
(STM32MP1xxD or STM32MP1xxF), and increase CPU voltage. To avoid
re-configuring I2C and PMIC before and after applying clock tree,
always boot at 650MHz, which is the frequency for nominal voltage.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git f75dbcd1ac71d67b51f88e2d0c0278558e113ad3 feat(stm32mp1): always boot at 650MHz]
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Id05a3ee17e7dd57e2d64dc06f8f1e7f9cb21e110
---
